{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     home/training-cta — the one thing the homepage asks you to do.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     This replaced the four-card .ns-path band that used to sit here. That
     band showed four stages as a grid of entrances, which is a good band on
     /training/ — and it is exactly what /training/ is for. On the HOMEPAGE it
     was the map AND the page under the map, so the reader chose a stage here
     and landed on a page that asked them to choose again.

     One band, one ask, one link. Everything about what the curriculum
     contains lives one click away and is written from real Ghost content
     rather than restated here.

     ⚠ THE COUNTS ARE READ FROM GHOST. Nothing here is typed: if there are no
     modules published the band still renders and simply does not claim a
     number. A homepage that advertises "24 modules" while the curriculum is
     empty is the fastest way to lose the trust the rest of the page builds.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--sunken">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">
        <div class="ns-band__head ns-band__head--between">
            <div>
                <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "Start training"}}</span>
                <h2 class="ns-band__title">{{t "One ordered path, from your first org to code you can defend"}}</h2>
                <p class="ns-band__lede">{{t "Written training you read at your own pace. Free, and being written in the open — start at the top if you are new, jump in if you are not."}}</p>

                <div class="ns-band__actions">
                    <a class="ns-btn ns-btn--primary" href="{{@site.url}}/training/">
                        {{> "icons/graduation-cap"}} {{t "Start training"}}
                    </a>
                    {{#get "posts" filter="tag:[hash-training-module,hash-training-section]" limit="1"}}
                        {{#if pagination.total}}
                            <span class="ns-kicker">{{pagination.total}} {{t "modules published"}}</span>
                        {{/if}}
                    {{/get}}
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
